https://static.warthunder.com/upload/image/!%20new/968%20-%20various%20news%20pictures/tables_d7ef803577a0f4b4dff61f816bc8d4bb.jpg


 Now loading a ground army is only possible when the helicopter and transport army(e.g. landing craft) is stationary.
 A single helicopter army now always fights a ground army in auto mode. You will still be able to send helicopters as reinforcements to a battle involving ground armies.
 Balance changes to the “Battle for the Fulda Gap” scenario:
USSR ground army:
MBT: 70 → 60;
Combat vehicles: 30 → 40;
USSR infantry army:
Combat vehicles: 15 → 30;
Germany infantry army:
MBT: 10 → 20;
Combat vehicles: 15 → 20;
Initial starting USSR fighters: 100 → 70.
German MBT units: The Leopard I has been removed from the list of available vehicles; the M48A2 G A2 has been set as  the default vehicle.
German infantry armies have been deployed to sectors  E3 and F5.
The current provided changelog reflects the major changes within the game as part of this Update. Some updates, additions and fixes may not be listed in the provided notes. War Thunder is constantly improving and specific fixes may be implemented without the client being updated.

